[Event "Knight School"]
[Opening "Owen Defence"]
[Variation "Owen Defence: Matovinsky Gambit"]
[ECO "B00"]
[Character "tactical"]
[Risk "medium"]
[EarlyMate "white"]
[Tricks "trap,pawn-grab,discovered-attack"]
[Refutes "1. e4 b6 2. d4 Bb7 3. Bd3 f5 4. exf5 Bxg2"]
[Themes "queen-check,bishop-on-d3"]
[Kind "for-us"]

1. e4 b6 2. d4 Bb7 3. Bd3 f5?! { Attacks e4 a second time, but weakens Black's own king. } 4. exf5 { Takes the pawn and opens the diagonal from h5 to e8. } 4... Bxg2? { Greedy: the bishop takes a pawn and attacks the rook on h1, but it leaves the king uncovered. } 5. Qh5+ { Check. The queen reaches the king because f7 is empty. } 5... g6 6. fxg6 { Threatens gxh7 and keeps up the attack. } 6... Nf6? { Hits the queen, but it walks into a mating net. } 7. gxh7+ { Discovered check: the pawn leaves g6 and the queen on h5 gives check down the diagonal. Black can take the queen, but the king is about to be trapped. } 7... Nxh5 8. Bg6# { Checkmate: nothing can take the bishop, and Black's own pieces box in the king. } *
